High level implementation plan

1) Validate function_ref and API contract
   - Locate WAN2MigrationManager.set_site_variable implementation (or implement it).
   - Confirm public method signature, expected types, return values, and error shapes.

2) CLI/menu wiring
   - Add new menu entry (ID 103) into the menu dispatcher and implement a handler function that gathers inputs and calls the manager.
   - Provide both an interactive and a non-interactive code path (flags for dry-run and force to support automation).

3) Input validation & interactive prompts
   - Implement site selection helper (reuse existing site-select helpers) to obtain site_id and site_name.
   - Validate variable_name and variable_value (type checking; optionally provide a whitelist for well-known keys like 'wan2_interface_enabled').
   - Implement confirmation prompt showing old_value -> new_value (skipped with --force).

4) Call into WAN2MigrationManager
   - Construct parameters and call WAN2MigrationManager.set_site_variable.
   - Support dry-run by calling a validate-only path if available; otherwise, simulate and show what would change.

5) Logging, audit, and feedback
   - Log both success and failure with full context.
   - Display clear success/failure messages to the user.

6) Tests & docs
   - Unit tests for validation and wiring (mock WAN2MigrationManager).
   - Integration tests if possible (against a staging API or by mocking mistapi client).
   - Add spec markdown under specs\\103-audit-menu-103-set-wan2-site-variable
   - Update README or menu help text.

7) Release considerations
   - Backwards compatibility: ensure existing workflows not impacted.
   - If site variables affect templates, coordinate rollouts.

Estimated timeline (small feature)
- Discovery & signature validation: 0.5 day
- Implementation (menu + validation + call): 1.5 days
- Tests & docs: 0.5 day
- Review & tweaks: 0.5 day
Total: ~3 days (approx)
